1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:03,044
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,386 --> 00:00:12,721
<i>Nimfa!</i>

3
00:00:12,804 --> 00:00:15,348
[Camia] <i>I don't know if I can</i>
<i>still trust you after this.</i>

4
00:00:15,432 --> 00:00:18,268
<i>Miss Camia, I'm begging you!</i>

5
00:00:18,351 --> 00:00:20,478
<i>Please, don't fire me.</i>

6
00:00:20,562 --> 00:00:21,980
[supporters] <i>Diego, Diego!</i>

7
00:00:22,063 --> 00:00:26,735
<i>You are the queen of hired killers</i>
<i>and hired rapists in this place!</i>

8
00:00:26,818 --> 00:00:30,321
<i>Why would you even think</i>
<i>that Ivy would be supporting us</i>

9
00:00:30,405 --> 00:00:32,574
<i>if she knew that I was the one</i>
<i>who tried to have her raped?</i>

10
00:00:32,657 --> 00:00:36,619
[Ivy] <i>I'm only here to support my Arnaldo.</i>

11
00:00:36,703 --> 00:00:41,833
[Emilia] <i>Didn't you tell me</i>
<i>Diego's party wouldn't make it?</i>

12
00:00:41,916 --> 00:00:43,460
[Nimfa] <i>Don't worry, Ma'am Emilia.</i>

13
00:00:43,543 --> 00:00:45,378
<i>I'm already working on it.</i>

14
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:47,213
[screams]

15
00:00:47,297 --> 00:00:51,217
<i>One of our security personnel</i>
<i>is betraying us.</i>

16
00:00:51,301 --> 00:00:54,971
<i>I want you to investigate,</i>
<i>and, if possible,</i>

17
00:00:55,055 --> 00:00:59,684
<i>annihilate this creature</i>
<i>who calls himself "Jaguar."</i>

18
00:00:59,768 --> 00:01:01,311
[Raul] <i>I'm going to your hideout</i>

19
00:01:01,394 --> 00:01:03,772
<i>because Julio gave me an order</i>
<i>to annihilate every one of you.</i>

20
00:01:03,855 --> 00:01:07,776
[Rufo] <i>Relax. All we need to do</i>
<i>is prepare for their arrival.</i>

21
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:09,235
[loud explosion]

22
00:01:09,319 --> 00:01:11,279
[Loring] <i>Diego! This wasn't an accident.</i>

23
00:01:11,362 --> 00:01:14,324
<i>They made it look like</i>
<i>the house caught fire,</i>

24
00:01:14,407 --> 00:01:18,161
<i>but they took our money!</i>
<i>They took everything!</i>

25
00:01:18,244 --> 00:01:20,622
[Emilia] <i>Through this, we will prove</i>

26
00:01:20,705 --> 00:01:23,333
<i>if Ivy Aguas is Camia's backer.</i>

27
00:01:23,416 --> 00:01:26,127
[Raul] <i>Papa. Looks like Jaguar</i>
<i>got ahead of us.</i>

28
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:29,297
-<i>Most of our men were killed.</i>
-[Julio] <i>What?!</i>

29
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:33,468
[Emilia] <i>I just got some information that</i>
<i>they're headed to Senator Magno,</i>

30
00:01:33,551 --> 00:01:36,221
<i>so you have to set up an appointment</i>
<i>and beat them to it.</i>

31
00:01:36,304 --> 00:01:38,765
[Diego] <i>Are you saying</i>
<i>Nimfa stole our funds?</i>

32
00:01:38,848 --> 00:01:40,141
[Nimfa] <i>Are you suggesting I did this?</i>

33
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:42,310
<i>What if the Ardientes</i>
<i>really are using you?</i>

34
00:01:42,393 --> 00:01:44,062
<i>I'm not their lapdog!</i>

35
00:01:44,145 --> 00:01:46,856
[Julio] <i>You bastard! Jaguar, you bastard!</i>

36
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:50,985
<i>Find the families of all our</i>
<i>former men who betrayed us.</i>

37
00:01:54,364 --> 00:01:55,698
[Arnaldo] To our success.

38
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:58,451
To my fiancé.

39
00:01:58,535 --> 00:02:00,578
To my future governor.

40
00:02:03,373 --> 00:02:05,250
Come to think of it, hon.

41
00:02:05,333 --> 00:02:10,755
It's like the universe
is telling us that you'll win,

42
00:02:10,839 --> 00:02:13,508
and the other candidate won't be
so lucky during the campaign.

43
00:02:14,884 --> 00:02:19,472
Well, everything that's been happening

44
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:22,267
is part of an intricate handiwork.

45
00:02:24,477 --> 00:02:25,812
What do you mean?

46
00:02:26,688 --> 00:02:28,940
Well, it's not my secret
to tell, hon. Sorry.

47
00:02:32,193 --> 00:02:34,404
Honey. Hon!

48
00:02:35,029 --> 00:02:38,199
I'm your fiancée, and soon to be…

49
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:40,410
Mrs. Torillo.

50
00:02:40,493 --> 00:02:44,873
So, I think it's my right
to know everything.

51
00:02:48,042 --> 00:02:49,210
Okay, sure.

52
00:02:49,544 --> 00:02:52,964
Let's just say we anticipate
Diego's every move.

53
00:02:53,047 --> 00:02:55,508
We just found out that
he'll be going to Magno…

54
00:02:55,884 --> 00:02:57,093
for financial backing.

55
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:02,807
There's a spy…

56
00:03:04,350 --> 00:03:05,768
in Diego's camp?

57
00:03:07,312 --> 00:03:13,026
And are you saying that you had
Loring's house burned down?

58
00:03:14,068 --> 00:03:15,528
Maybe yes, maybe no.

59
00:03:16,988 --> 00:03:19,824
But one thing's for sure,
we're a political family.

60
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:24,245
And we have been doing this
for many years.

61
00:03:25,788 --> 00:03:28,416
We're good at it.
No, actually, we're experts.

62
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:34,213
Okay? So if there's one thing
that I can assure you…

63
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:38,468
It doesn't matter who's up
against the Ardientes because…

64
00:03:40,136 --> 00:03:41,054
we're gonna win.

65
00:03:42,847 --> 00:03:46,059
Whatever it takes, we're gonna win.

66
00:03:52,565 --> 00:03:55,568
[upbeat music playing]

67
00:04:29,477 --> 00:04:32,438
[tense music playing]

68
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:52,083
-Ivy.
-Diego.

69
00:04:55,086 --> 00:04:57,380
They burned down Aunt Loring's house.

70
00:04:57,463 --> 00:05:00,341
Our campaign funding is gone, all of it.

71
00:05:00,425 --> 00:05:02,302
But we'll come up with something.

72
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:04,595
We'll ask for help
from Senator Magno's party.

73
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:15,398
[suspenseful music playing]

74
00:05:54,979 --> 00:05:57,982
[suspenseful music playing]

75
00:06:08,326 --> 00:06:10,912
Diego, I know what happened
to Mrs. Loring's house.

76
00:06:12,997 --> 00:06:16,000
The Ardientes want to get
to Senator Magno first.

77
00:06:16,375 --> 00:06:18,836
Especially now that they know
your funds are gone.

78
00:06:19,170 --> 00:06:22,298
They know you'll ask help
from Senator Magno.

79
00:06:23,549 --> 00:06:26,052
We'll plan our approach to their party.

80
00:06:26,803 --> 00:06:30,431
I'll make sure they choose us.
Not the Ardientes.

81
00:06:35,269 --> 00:06:38,397
[suspenseful music playing]

82
00:07:08,094 --> 00:07:09,095
Hon?

83
00:07:11,305 --> 00:07:14,308
[suspenseful music playing]

84
00:07:29,699 --> 00:07:30,825
Arnaldo!

85
00:07:31,534 --> 00:07:33,035
Uh… Hon!

86
00:07:33,703 --> 00:07:35,872
What are you doing there?
That's my office.

87
00:07:36,789 --> 00:07:39,333
Well, uh… I was looking for you.

88
00:07:39,792 --> 00:07:41,294
-Hmm?
-I was looking for you.

89
00:07:41,377 --> 00:07:43,212
You were gone when I woke up.
Where'd you go?

90
00:07:43,754 --> 00:07:45,214
Well… Morning run.

91
00:07:47,550 --> 00:07:49,510
But why did you lock the door?

92
00:07:51,804 --> 00:07:55,516
Oh, yes. Sorry, hon. Force of habit.

93
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:58,060
You see, after what happened
to Nanny Carlotta,

94
00:07:58,144 --> 00:08:00,897
I'm afraid someone might come in
and kill me too.

95
00:08:01,606 --> 00:08:03,858
So, I'm sorry if I locked the door.

96
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:07,028
Anyway, are you hungry?

97
00:08:07,612 --> 00:08:09,197
I'll cook you breakfast.

98
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:11,741
-Yeah, I'm starving.
-Let's go.

99
00:08:17,622 --> 00:08:19,290
Well, Camia.

100
00:08:23,169 --> 00:08:25,213
How did you find out we were here?

101
00:08:25,838 --> 00:08:27,048
Wow, how rude.

102
00:08:27,131 --> 00:08:29,467
Well, what makes you think
that you're the only one

103
00:08:29,550 --> 00:08:31,469
who thought of coming to Senator Magno?

104
00:08:31,552 --> 00:08:32,887
Have you forgotten?

105
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:34,555
We used to belong to the same party.

106
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:36,516
It's only natural to ask for his help

107
00:08:36,599 --> 00:08:38,309
regarding Arnaldo's candidacy.

108
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:41,771
Correct. We are here to strike a deal.

109
00:08:42,563 --> 00:08:44,398
Some kind of a partnership.

110
00:08:44,482 --> 00:08:47,985
Unlike you guys, I know you're
only here to ask for funds.

111
00:08:48,069 --> 00:08:49,445
-Right?
-[Emilia] Mm-hm.

112
00:08:50,154 --> 00:08:52,490
Didn't you leave Magno's political party?

113
00:08:53,449 --> 00:08:55,243
You can no longer earn the trust

114
00:08:55,326 --> 00:08:57,078
of the party you once took for granted.

115
00:08:58,037 --> 00:09:01,415
And you've been stupid
and cowardly since we were kids.

116
00:09:01,832 --> 00:09:04,210
I don't think there's
much difference now, okay?

117
00:09:04,585 --> 00:09:07,505
So you have the right
to lecture us about politics

118
00:09:07,588 --> 00:09:09,173
because you haven't proven yourself yet.

119
00:09:10,258 --> 00:09:13,052
I'm grateful you didn't teach
me anything about politics.

120
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:17,473
Because if you had,
I'd be ashamed of myself.

121
00:09:20,268 --> 00:09:21,477
You know, hon?

122
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:26,482
I think it's better if we
just ignore those peasants.

123
00:09:27,775 --> 00:09:29,110
Right? Let's go.

124
00:09:29,193 --> 00:09:32,780
-Great idea. Let's go.
-Excuse us.

125
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,324
[Arnaldo] Excuse me.

126
00:09:42,206 --> 00:09:45,376
So, can we count on
the full support of your party?

127
00:09:45,668 --> 00:09:48,588
There's a reason why we've
already parted ways.

128
00:09:49,297 --> 00:09:50,381
What do you mean, Senator?

129
00:09:50,923 --> 00:09:53,676
I guess it's better to leave
things as they are, Emilia.

130
00:09:54,051 --> 00:09:57,305
And which candidate will you
accept into your party, Senator?

131
00:09:57,680 --> 00:10:01,267
I would love to get to know
your other son better.

132
00:10:01,684 --> 00:10:03,978
Well, excuse me, Senator,
but he's not my son,

133
00:10:04,061 --> 00:10:07,690
and I cannot believe that you're
even considering that bastard.

134
00:10:08,482 --> 00:10:10,610
Everything is still under consideration.

135
00:10:12,069 --> 00:10:13,070
Well then, okay.

136
00:10:13,154 --> 00:10:15,281
Thank you for
your time, Senator. Let's go.

137
00:10:21,078 --> 00:10:24,123
If you think all I'll do is
shout at you through the phone,

138
00:10:24,206 --> 00:10:27,627
then, you're wrong.
You worthless piece of trash!

139
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:31,631
Ma'am, how can I be worthless
when I sabotaged Diego's plans?

140
00:10:32,256 --> 00:10:34,091
You're the worthless one
because up until now,

141
00:10:34,175 --> 00:10:35,551
you haven't paid me yet!

142
00:10:36,010 --> 00:10:39,513
If you don't pay me, I'll expose you!

143
00:10:39,597 --> 00:10:41,641
Is that all you want?

144
00:10:42,099 --> 00:10:44,435
Fine, stuff these down your throat!

145
00:10:44,852 --> 00:10:46,854
Go, pick them up!

146
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:50,566
It's my turn
for some blackmail now. Come here.

147
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:51,901
[squeals]

148
00:10:52,443 --> 00:10:54,612
[groans]

149
00:10:54,695 --> 00:10:56,906
Do you know who you're dealing with?

150
00:10:56,989 --> 00:10:59,450
You are dealing with Emilia Ardiente.

151
00:10:59,533 --> 00:11:03,245
I can have you killed and make
it look like it was an accident!

152
00:11:03,329 --> 00:11:05,498
Do you understand?! Come here!

153
00:11:05,956 --> 00:11:10,711
I'm giving you until tonight
to finish your job.

154
00:11:10,795 --> 00:11:13,005
Or else… Do you see that toilet?

155
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:16,008
That's the last thing
you'll see before you die,

156
00:11:16,092 --> 00:11:17,927
you piece of shit!

157
00:11:19,929 --> 00:11:20,930
[weeps]

158
00:11:26,143 --> 00:11:27,186
Miss Ivy.

159
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:30,856
[tense music playing]

160
00:11:35,277 --> 00:11:36,487
Oh, Ivy.

161
00:11:36,946 --> 00:11:39,740
I thought you left with Arnaldo.
Why are you still here?

162
00:11:41,992 --> 00:11:43,702
-I need to go.
-Are you okay?

163
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:49,166
I'm all right.

164
00:11:50,126 --> 00:11:51,043
Nimfa.

165
00:11:52,461 --> 00:11:55,464
[suspenseful music playing]

166
00:12:09,812 --> 00:12:13,274
Here. Use these to wipe your face.

167
00:12:16,777 --> 00:12:17,778
Thank you.

168
00:12:20,823 --> 00:12:24,410
-I'm leaving too.
-Not so fast, Emilia.

169
00:12:25,703 --> 00:12:29,206
You need to tell me
what that woman did to you.

170
00:12:30,332 --> 00:12:33,627
I know we don't get along sometimes.

171
00:12:35,004 --> 00:12:39,008
Is she hurting you? Just tell me if so

172
00:12:39,091 --> 00:12:42,678
because I don't want anyone
to hurt my future mother-in-law.

173
00:12:43,929 --> 00:12:46,765
And what makes you say that, Ivy?

174
00:12:47,349 --> 00:12:50,311
You think that someone like me

175
00:12:50,394 --> 00:12:52,730
would lose to that uncouth peasant?!

176
00:12:52,813 --> 00:12:53,689
[scoffs]

177
00:12:53,772 --> 00:12:58,986
You know, Ivy, I may have said
that her fashion sense sucks

178
00:12:59,069 --> 00:13:01,030
and that I hate that she's Diego's ally,

179
00:13:01,113 --> 00:13:02,072
but that's it.

180
00:13:02,156 --> 00:13:04,200
Nothing more, and nothing less.

181
00:13:04,950 --> 00:13:06,076
You know me, Ivy.

182
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:10,039
I love bullying people
with low self-esteem.

183
00:13:10,623 --> 00:13:12,208
[both chuckle]

184
00:13:13,125 --> 00:13:15,336
So that's why you can't bully me.

185
00:13:18,797 --> 00:13:19,840
I'll go ahead.

186
00:13:19,924 --> 00:13:22,092
Bye, future mother-in-law.

187
00:13:26,055 --> 00:13:27,890
Bye, my daughter-in-law.

188
00:13:27,973 --> 00:13:28,974
Aww.

189
00:13:44,782 --> 00:13:46,909
Was it management…

190
00:13:48,077 --> 00:13:49,161
the money…

191
00:13:50,496 --> 00:13:55,584
or… the change of view, the environment?

192
00:13:56,961 --> 00:14:00,130
Which of those things
I mentioned is the reason…

193
00:14:01,924 --> 00:14:05,177
why you switched to Jaguar's side?

194
00:14:05,719 --> 00:14:08,097
[stutters] I was just blinded,
Congressman.

195
00:14:08,764 --> 00:14:10,641
I was forced to do it
because of my colleagues.

196
00:14:10,724 --> 00:14:13,894
Besides, Jaguar has a lot of money.

197
00:14:14,562 --> 00:14:17,064
His money's like water
in the ocean, it's endless!

198
00:14:19,692 --> 00:14:20,693
Well…

199
00:14:22,319 --> 00:14:26,782
Where is this fountain of wealth located?

200
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:29,118
At the old hideout.

201
00:14:30,286 --> 00:14:31,287
[exhales sharply]

202
00:14:32,997 --> 00:14:35,499
Where is this old hideout?

203
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:38,669
First, you have to promise me
that you'll really give me

204
00:14:38,752 --> 00:14:40,629
that new house and land in Manila,

205
00:14:40,713 --> 00:14:43,340
where my family and I can start anew.

206
00:14:47,511 --> 00:14:51,140
Inside this envelope, you'll find the keys

207
00:14:51,223 --> 00:14:52,808
to a brand new car…

208
00:14:53,893 --> 00:14:57,730
and the title
to a house and lot in Manila.

209
00:14:58,898 --> 00:15:00,107
You can check it.

210
00:15:00,190 --> 00:15:01,817
You can even have it investigated.

211
00:15:02,693 --> 00:15:04,945
Everything is under your name.

212
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:11,535
[Rufo] I'm sure Julio will get back at us.

213
00:15:12,202 --> 00:15:14,163
Especially now that he knows
where our hideout is.

214
00:15:14,830 --> 00:15:18,292
So? Are we supposed
to be afraid of him now?

215
00:15:18,667 --> 00:15:21,086
No matter how many times he comes here…

216
00:15:21,837 --> 00:15:24,131
he still won't be able to defeat
us. Because, first of all,

217
00:15:24,214 --> 00:15:26,133
Julio Ardiente doesn't have enough men.

218
00:15:27,217 --> 00:15:29,762
The Ardientes are powerless now.
They're weak.

219
00:15:31,138 --> 00:15:37,811
So, now, it's time for you
to hold up your end of the deal.

220
00:15:40,439 --> 00:15:43,817
Where can I find Jaguar?

221
00:15:44,485 --> 00:15:46,862
At the old hideout in the town of Gulod.

222
00:15:51,408 --> 00:15:52,952
-[suppressed gunshot]
-[grunts]

223
00:15:56,789 --> 00:15:57,831
Idiot.

224
00:15:58,832 --> 00:16:00,960
That's what you get for believing in me.

225
00:16:02,169 --> 00:16:03,170
But now I know.

226
00:16:04,505 --> 00:16:07,007
Jaguar's at his old hideout…

227
00:16:08,092 --> 00:16:09,927
in the town of Gulod.

228
00:16:11,845 --> 00:16:13,222
Give me those documents.

229
00:16:14,139 --> 00:16:17,601
This bastard actually believed
I'd give him a house and lot.

230
00:16:19,645 --> 00:16:20,688
Fool.

231
00:16:21,063 --> 00:16:23,357
And clean up the mess he made.

232
00:16:32,783 --> 00:16:35,577
Well, well, Mister Jaguar…

233
00:16:37,579 --> 00:16:39,581
I guess I'll see you soon.

234
00:16:43,669 --> 00:16:46,213
Yes, Senator. I'm not an Ardiente.

235
00:16:48,632 --> 00:16:52,094
I was never treated like
an Ardiente by my own family.

236
00:16:53,137 --> 00:16:54,346
And when I was a kid,

237
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:57,391
I saw just how
they treated my friend's family.

238
00:16:58,225 --> 00:17:02,271
<i>You killed my husband!</i>
<i>You killed him! Get out of here!</i>

239
00:17:02,354 --> 00:17:03,939
<i>Mom, calm down.</i>

240
00:17:04,982 --> 00:17:07,693
[Ivy] <i>Your mother, that rapist Raul,</i>

241
00:17:07,776 --> 00:17:10,571
<i>the people who rule Poblacion Ardiente…</i>

242
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:15,242
<i>they had us slaughtered</i>
<i>like we were animals.</i>

243
00:17:16,285 --> 00:17:17,828
[Diego] <i>I saw the struggles of all those</i>

244
00:17:17,911 --> 00:17:19,747
<i>families who worked the fields.</i>

245
00:17:19,830 --> 00:17:22,958
<i>You can't take away our land!</i>
<i>We won't back down!</i>

246
00:17:23,042 --> 00:17:25,753
[clamoring]

247
00:17:26,462 --> 00:17:29,757
And, because of that,
I started to build my dream.

248
00:17:31,008 --> 00:17:35,012
I promised myself that, one day,
a new government will rise.

249
00:17:35,763 --> 00:17:37,931
There will be leaders who'll truly care

250
00:17:38,015 --> 00:17:39,475
about the residents of Ardiente.

251
00:17:40,934 --> 00:17:44,772
I'll admit that I still have a
lot to learn about politics.

252
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:48,525
And we chose your political party…

253
00:17:49,068 --> 00:17:51,070
because we believe in you the most.

254
00:17:51,361 --> 00:17:53,447
What if we believe in something

255
00:17:53,530 --> 00:17:55,699
that goes against your principles?

256
00:17:58,660 --> 00:17:59,828
I may be new to this…

257
00:18:00,996 --> 00:18:02,539
but I'm not innocent.

258
00:18:03,332 --> 00:18:06,794
I know that friendships
don't last in politics…

259
00:18:07,628 --> 00:18:09,421
especially if two parties
no longer believe

260
00:18:09,505 --> 00:18:10,547
in the same thing.

261
00:18:12,091 --> 00:18:14,802
But as long as we help
each other out this election…

262
00:18:15,219 --> 00:18:18,388
I have a feeling
that we'll get along well.

263
00:18:20,224 --> 00:18:22,142
I'm lucky because you chose
to approach me.

264
00:18:23,894 --> 00:18:25,437
Welcome to the party.

265
00:18:28,148 --> 00:18:31,568
-Senator, thank you very much.
-My pleasure.

266
00:18:32,111 --> 00:18:34,780
-Thank you.
-[Marlon] Thank you, Senator.

267
00:18:37,324 --> 00:18:39,743
-Batch, Aunt Camia.
-Congratulations, Diego.

268
00:18:43,288 --> 00:18:46,291
[suspenseful music playing]

269
00:19:03,684 --> 00:19:05,144
-[gunfire]
-[grunts]

270
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:08,188
[gunfire]

271
00:19:15,404 --> 00:19:18,657
-Jaguar! Jaguar!
-[gunfire]

272
00:19:19,616 --> 00:19:21,660
-What's the matter?
-Jaguar, Julio's men are here.

273
00:19:22,327 --> 00:19:27,875
[gunfire]

274
00:19:28,208 --> 00:19:29,877
How did they find out where we are?

275
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:32,296
Some of the Ardientes' men
switched back to their side.

276
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:34,548
Jaguar, let's go.

277
00:19:34,631 --> 00:19:36,508
No, we'll fight back.

278
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:40,262
[gunfire]

279
00:19:40,345 --> 00:19:41,430
Jaguar!

280
00:19:42,848 --> 00:19:43,849
Jaguar!

281
00:19:45,726 --> 00:19:48,604
You may have lured my people…

282
00:19:49,188 --> 00:19:50,647
with your riches.

283
00:19:53,525 --> 00:19:57,112
But do you know what the
greatest motivator in life is?

284
00:19:58,780 --> 00:19:59,781
Fear!

285
00:20:00,866 --> 00:20:03,160
Fear for your own life.

286
00:20:03,785 --> 00:20:06,246
Fear for the lives of your loved ones.

287
00:20:08,207 --> 00:20:10,334
[Julio] <i>The fear of death.</i>

288
00:20:20,677 --> 00:20:21,511
<i>Come with us.</i>

289
00:20:21,595 --> 00:20:23,180
<i>Don't kill my family, Congressman!</i>

290
00:20:23,263 --> 00:20:27,768
<i>-Don't kill them!</i>
<i>-Congressman, have mercy on us.</i>

291
00:20:29,978 --> 00:20:31,855
<i>I'll join the group again, Congressman.</i>

292
00:20:32,814 --> 00:20:35,067
<i>I'll do everything you ask, Congressman.</i>

293
00:20:35,150 --> 00:20:37,236
<i>Just don't kill my family.</i>

294
00:20:37,861 --> 00:20:39,696
<i>I'm fairly easy to talk to.</i>

295
00:20:40,906 --> 00:20:43,492
-[gunshot]
<i>-My son!</i>

296
00:20:43,951 --> 00:20:47,246
<i>Congressman! Don't kill my entire family!</i>

297
00:20:47,788 --> 00:20:49,915
<i>It wasn't me. It was him.</i>

298
00:20:49,998 --> 00:20:52,876
[sobs]

299
00:20:53,377 --> 00:20:55,087
[man] <i>I'll go back to the group.</i>

300
00:20:55,879 --> 00:20:57,839
<i>Just don't kill my entire family!</i>

301
00:20:58,799 --> 00:21:02,719
<i>Congressman. I beg you, Congressman.</i>

302
00:21:03,804 --> 00:21:06,515
[woman yowls]

303
00:21:08,475 --> 00:21:10,602
Jaguar! Come out!

304
00:21:12,646 --> 00:21:13,689
I'm here!

305
00:21:16,608 --> 00:21:17,693
Face me.

306
00:21:20,737 --> 00:21:22,698
[gunfire]

307
00:21:31,790 --> 00:21:33,500
Put your guns down. Now!

308
00:21:45,971 --> 00:21:48,015
[gunfire]

309
00:21:48,682 --> 00:21:52,853
[gunfire]

310
00:21:54,771 --> 00:21:57,774
[tense music playing]

311
00:22:02,779 --> 00:22:03,697
Hurry, come on!

312
00:22:25,969 --> 00:22:27,220
-What happened?
-Here they come.

313
00:22:31,099 --> 00:22:32,309
Folks…

314
00:22:34,061 --> 00:22:35,187
I have good news.

315
00:22:35,270 --> 00:22:37,898
Diego was chosen to be part
of the senator's party.

316
00:22:37,981 --> 00:22:39,900
[cheers]

317
00:22:40,233 --> 00:22:43,904
That's amazing! We finally have a backer.

318
00:22:43,987 --> 00:22:46,073
Diego is finally in an electoral party.

319
00:22:46,156 --> 00:22:49,326
Not only that, Auntie. We're
going to repair your house.

320
00:22:49,993 --> 00:22:53,747
And Senator Magno promised us
our own headquarters too.

321
00:22:53,830 --> 00:22:56,208
-That's great!
-That's great news!

322
00:22:56,291 --> 00:22:57,834
We're so proud of you, Diego!

323
00:22:58,502 --> 00:22:59,586
Thanks, Uncle.

324
00:23:00,170 --> 00:23:04,466
I hope our partnership with
Senator Magno's party goes well.

325
00:23:05,008 --> 00:23:07,677
-Boss, congrats.
-Thanks.

326
00:23:08,345 --> 00:23:11,181
-Congratulations again, Diego.
-Thanks, Aunt Camia.

327
00:23:11,681 --> 00:23:13,391
-Batch.
-Miss Camia, thank you.

328
00:23:13,475 --> 00:23:15,018
-Congrats.
-Congrats.

329
00:23:15,936 --> 00:23:17,521
-[Camia] Excellent!
-Well, Batch won!

330
00:23:17,604 --> 00:23:18,772
[indistinct lively chatter]

331
00:23:25,654 --> 00:23:27,697
Raul, are you okay?

332
00:23:27,781 --> 00:23:28,782
[groans]

333
00:23:35,413 --> 00:23:37,040
-[Rufo] Jaguar…
-[Raul sighs]

334
00:23:37,624 --> 00:23:38,583
[Natalie gasps]

335
00:23:38,667 --> 00:23:40,544
What do we do? What should I do?

336
00:23:43,421 --> 00:23:46,550
[groans]

337
00:23:47,592 --> 00:23:49,511
This shouldn't have happened to me.

338
00:23:50,303 --> 00:23:53,807
Soon enough, Emilia will know I'm Jaguar.

339
00:23:53,890 --> 00:23:55,058
Open this.

340
00:23:55,642 --> 00:23:56,852
Hurry!

341
00:24:01,565 --> 00:24:02,774
Ouch! Careful.

342
00:24:02,858 --> 00:24:04,442
Please don't die on me.

343
00:24:09,573 --> 00:24:12,659
I'll do it! Just call the doctor!

344
00:24:22,043 --> 00:24:26,173
Stupid Magno! He'll regret
that he didn't choose Arnaldo.

345
00:24:26,256 --> 00:24:28,884
And if he chooses Diego instead,

346
00:24:28,967 --> 00:24:31,678
I can kill him, Aunt Claire.
I can kill him!

347
00:24:31,761 --> 00:24:32,971
Where's Papa?

348
00:24:34,014 --> 00:24:35,390
Hey, can you relax, Mom?

349
00:24:35,473 --> 00:24:39,477
There are many parties and donors
other than Magno's,

350
00:24:39,561 --> 00:24:40,729
so just relax.

351
00:24:41,313 --> 00:24:42,439
[Emilia sighs]

352
00:24:43,732 --> 00:24:46,776
[tense music playing]

353
00:25:16,306 --> 00:25:18,850
-Ma'am.
-Where should we deliver this?

354
00:25:20,060 --> 00:25:22,896
I can take you there, ma'am.
Ma'am, this way.

355
00:25:22,979 --> 00:25:23,980
Okay. Thanks.

356
00:25:26,942 --> 00:25:29,986
[tense music playing]

357
00:26:29,421 --> 00:26:32,716
[suspenseful music playing]

358
00:26:54,154 --> 00:26:56,114
[goon] Congressman… is this all right?

359
00:27:26,936 --> 00:27:28,271
Everything's set, Congressman.

360
00:27:33,693 --> 00:27:36,321
-[door shuts]
-[suspenseful music]

361
00:27:39,783 --> 00:27:40,742
Congressman.

362
00:27:42,077 --> 00:27:43,119
I'll be right back.

363
00:27:52,212 --> 00:27:53,505
Oh. Congressman…

364
00:27:53,588 --> 00:27:55,382
I was just leaving the money in here.

365
00:28:18,822 --> 00:28:21,658
Get those in order.
We're giving them away tomorrow.

366
00:28:22,617 --> 00:28:23,493
Excuse me.

367
00:28:23,576 --> 00:28:25,203
[Nimfa] What are you writing here?

368
00:28:25,286 --> 00:28:26,371
[volunteer] The first one?

369
00:28:26,454 --> 00:28:29,582
Those are the voters registered
in every precinct.

370
00:28:29,666 --> 00:28:30,708
[Nimfa] I see.

371
00:28:31,918 --> 00:28:32,669
[Marlon] Okay.

372
00:28:34,170 --> 00:28:35,380
[phone ringing]

373
00:28:37,382 --> 00:28:41,010
Hon. It's from Manila.
I have to take this.

374
00:28:41,094 --> 00:28:42,262
-Okay.
-It's Joanne.

375
00:28:42,345 --> 00:28:43,972
-Yes, Joanne?
-I'll just be here.

376
00:28:48,977 --> 00:28:50,019
Let's have coffee.

377
00:28:52,105 --> 00:28:53,565
Mom, what is it?

378
00:28:54,774 --> 00:28:57,986
Lily, Senator Magno chose Diego!

379
00:28:58,528 --> 00:28:59,612
<i>That's great news!</i>

380
00:28:59,696 --> 00:29:01,656
Where is he? Let me talk to him.

381
00:29:01,740 --> 00:29:03,366
He's not around…

382
00:29:03,450 --> 00:29:04,576
<i>But, Lily…</i>

383
00:29:04,659 --> 00:29:09,497
Thanks for helping out
with Diego's campaign.

384
00:29:09,998 --> 00:29:11,416
None of this would've happened…

385
00:29:11,499 --> 00:29:13,042
if it weren't for you.

386
00:29:14,294 --> 00:29:15,253
<i>Lily…</i>

387
00:29:15,336 --> 00:29:17,130
To be honest…

388
00:29:18,381 --> 00:29:21,342
I want nothing more than
to be with you at this moment.

389
00:29:21,426 --> 00:29:23,219
<i>It would've been nice to celebrate…</i>

390
00:29:23,303 --> 00:29:24,888
our successes together.

391
00:29:26,973 --> 00:29:28,725
But, I know that's not possible.

392
00:29:28,808 --> 00:29:32,145
Not until we bring the Ardientes down.

393
00:29:33,938 --> 00:29:37,358
We can't live like mother
and daughter yet…

394
00:29:38,610 --> 00:29:44,073
so, Lily, I'll make do with
working with you from afar.

395
00:29:46,534 --> 00:29:48,787
I miss you so much, Lily.

396
00:29:51,456 --> 00:29:52,457
[quietly] Lily?

397
00:29:52,540 --> 00:29:56,753
[tense music playing]

398
00:30:14,479 --> 00:30:16,022
[phone ringing]

399
00:30:16,105 --> 00:30:17,732
Excuse me. I have to take this call.

400
00:30:19,484 --> 00:30:22,070
Nimfa, Nimfa, Nimfa.

401
00:30:22,862 --> 00:30:27,075
What took you forever to call?
It's about time!

402
00:30:28,201 --> 00:30:32,747
So… what will it be? Dead or alive?

403
00:30:33,373 --> 00:30:35,333
Mom, could you look around you?

404
00:30:35,416 --> 00:30:38,086
What? Why, dear?

405
00:30:44,634 --> 00:30:46,594
See if there's anyone
keeping an eye on you.

406
00:30:48,805 --> 00:30:51,266
I don't think so, dear. Why?
What's the problem?

407
00:30:53,351 --> 00:30:55,061
I'm sorry, but I need to hang up now.

408
00:30:56,771 --> 00:30:58,398
Do you have an update on Camia?

409
00:30:58,773 --> 00:31:00,149
Nothing, Ma'am Emilia.

410
00:31:01,109 --> 00:31:02,944
But I found out something more important.

411
00:31:07,699 --> 00:31:08,700
[quietly] Mom.

412
00:31:09,784 --> 00:31:13,997
Just now, someone called Emilia
while we were on the phone.

413
00:31:14,455 --> 00:31:15,915
<i>That's why the Ardientes are always</i>

414
00:31:15,999 --> 00:31:17,792
<i>one step ahead of you and Diego…</i>

415
00:31:17,876 --> 00:31:20,753
because they planted a spy in your camp.

416
00:31:27,093 --> 00:31:29,262
Yes, Camia does have a backer.

417
00:31:30,805 --> 00:31:33,725
-Okay.
-But it's not Ivy Aguas.

418
00:31:34,142 --> 00:31:36,352
Huh? What do you mean?

419
00:31:37,395 --> 00:31:38,563
<i>Then…</i>

420
00:31:38,646 --> 00:31:39,522
who is it?

421
00:31:40,106 --> 00:31:40,940
<i>Ivy Aguas…</i>

422
00:31:41,024 --> 00:31:45,111
is the only possible person
connected to Camia Cruz, right?

423
00:31:45,570 --> 00:31:47,113
<i>She's her only possible backer.</i>

424
00:31:47,655 --> 00:31:48,907
So, who is it? Tell me.

425
00:31:48,990 --> 00:31:51,618
It's not Ivy Aguas.

426
00:31:52,201 --> 00:31:53,953
It's Camia's daughter.

427
00:31:54,829 --> 00:31:56,164
Lily Cruz!

428
00:31:56,956 --> 00:31:59,083
-What?
-You heard me!

429
00:31:59,834 --> 00:32:01,628
<i>Lily Cruz is alive!</i>

430
00:32:06,883 --> 00:32:09,969
No. That's not true.

431
00:32:10,678 --> 00:32:14,557
It can't be Lily Cruz. You are a liar.

432
00:32:15,016 --> 00:32:18,937
How can she help Camia
if she's already dead?

433
00:32:19,020 --> 00:32:22,357
She is dead as a doornail.
She can't be alive.

434
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:25,443
I'm sure of it. I heard Camia talking…

435
00:32:25,526 --> 00:32:27,153
<i>to Lily on the phone.</i>

436
00:32:27,236 --> 00:32:29,864
No. That is impossible.

437
00:32:30,198 --> 00:32:31,658
Completely impossible!

438
00:32:32,033 --> 00:32:32,992
[Camia] <i>I knew it.</i>

439
00:32:33,076 --> 00:32:35,787
Emilia has a spy in our camp.

440
00:32:35,870 --> 00:32:38,289
Mom, I need to hang up now.

441
00:32:39,040 --> 00:32:40,124
<i>I think Emilia's spy…</i>

442
00:32:40,208 --> 00:32:43,544
just discovered something.
I need to find out what it is.

443
00:32:43,628 --> 00:32:48,383
All right, dear. Be careful.
I'll tell Diego about this. Bye.

444
00:32:50,468 --> 00:32:52,679
[Nimfa] <i>She's alive, Ma'am</i>
<i>Emilia. She must know…</i>

445
00:32:52,762 --> 00:32:56,099
what's happening for her to back Camia.

446
00:32:56,182 --> 00:32:57,600
<i>Lily Cruz is alive.</i>

447
00:32:58,142 --> 00:33:00,645
And it's possible she's here
in Poblacion Ardiente.

448
00:33:00,728 --> 00:33:02,772
No! No!

449
00:33:03,690 --> 00:33:06,109
[ominous music playing]

450
00:33:06,192 --> 00:33:09,070
-Doc, thank you very much.
-He should be fine.

451
00:33:09,153 --> 00:33:11,739
If something happens, just call me.

452
00:33:11,823 --> 00:33:13,908
-Okay.
-Let's go, Doc.

453
00:33:18,204 --> 00:33:19,414
Ouch! Hey!

454
00:33:19,497 --> 00:33:20,790
I'm sorry.

455
00:33:25,044 --> 00:33:26,587
I'm so sorry, I just…

456
00:33:28,548 --> 00:33:31,342
Please don't pretend
like this is just a small bite.

457
00:33:32,093 --> 00:33:33,344
One way or the other,

458
00:33:33,428 --> 00:33:37,390
the Ardientes will find out
what you're really up to.

459
00:33:37,724 --> 00:33:40,810
They'll catch you, and they will
crush you like a fly.

460
00:33:41,519 --> 00:33:42,770
What do you want me to do?

461
00:33:44,355 --> 00:33:46,232
I don't know. Well…

462
00:33:46,315 --> 00:33:48,484
Maybe you can… stay here?

463
00:33:48,818 --> 00:33:50,111
Let me take care of you?

464
00:33:51,654 --> 00:33:52,697
Please?

465
00:33:55,783 --> 00:33:57,910
[Claire] Emilia, what's wrong?
You look pale.

466
00:34:05,001 --> 00:34:07,879
[suspenseful music playing]

467
00:34:13,009 --> 00:34:14,844
Lily Cruz is alive, Aunt Claire.

468
00:34:16,095 --> 00:34:19,640
She's Camia's backer. She's alive.

469
00:34:20,224 --> 00:34:21,684
Lily Cruz is alive.

470
00:34:22,101 --> 00:34:24,395
Lily Cruz? Camia's daughter?

471
00:34:25,188 --> 00:34:26,064
That can't be.

472
00:34:26,147 --> 00:34:29,067
That girl has been rotting
in her grave for 13 years now!

473
00:34:29,776 --> 00:34:31,903
Yes. She is alive.

474
00:34:31,986 --> 00:34:34,363
And she's helping Camia now.

475
00:34:34,447 --> 00:34:36,824
She's her backer.

476
00:34:36,908 --> 00:34:39,660
This is not happening!
This is not happening!

477
00:34:41,162 --> 00:34:42,914
-<i>Do you have the child?</i>
-[social worker] <i>Yes, ma'am.</i>

478
00:34:43,706 --> 00:34:46,959
<i>You know what to do. Finish her off.</i>

479
00:34:47,043 --> 00:34:48,211
[young Lily] <i>Please let me go!</i>

480
00:34:48,294 --> 00:34:49,378
[gunshot]

481
00:34:53,049 --> 00:34:54,717
She can't be alive, Aunt Claire!

482
00:34:55,343 --> 00:34:56,803
She cannot be alive!

483
00:34:56,886 --> 00:35:02,683
This isn't true.
Lily Cruz is dead! She's dead!

484
00:35:03,017 --> 00:35:04,227
She's dead!

485
00:35:05,061 --> 00:35:06,604
-Mom!
-Emilia!

486
00:35:06,687 --> 00:35:08,940
-Emilia!
-[Arnaldo] Water!

487
00:35:10,108 --> 00:35:11,150
Get us some water!

488
00:35:18,157 --> 00:35:20,159
Jaguar, while you're recovering,

489
00:35:20,243 --> 00:35:21,994
I'll ask my boss for help.

490
00:35:22,703 --> 00:35:25,623
You should. We lost a lot of men.

491
00:35:25,706 --> 00:35:28,042
We need to get back at Julio.

492
00:35:28,126 --> 00:35:31,337
My boss promised to send us more men.

493
00:35:31,420 --> 00:35:35,091
People who can help us
gain more money and power.

494
00:35:35,716 --> 00:35:36,843
Your boss can do that?

495
00:35:38,261 --> 00:35:40,429
I need to meet him.

496
00:35:42,974 --> 00:35:45,393
Jaguar, in due time.

497
00:35:53,151 --> 00:35:55,778
Emilia! Emilia! Emilia!

498
00:35:56,445 --> 00:35:58,156
-Mm?
-Emilia! Are you still alive?

499
00:35:58,656 --> 00:36:01,075
You're a buzzkill, my girl.

500
00:36:02,285 --> 00:36:05,955
Do you know I just got my men
back from the gambling den?

501
00:36:06,038 --> 00:36:08,416
I should be celebrating right now.

502
00:36:08,499 --> 00:36:11,043
But here I am in your room,

503
00:36:11,127 --> 00:36:14,046
checking if you're still alive or dead.

504
00:36:14,797 --> 00:36:17,592
I'm still alive, Papa. Alive and kicking.

505
00:36:17,675 --> 00:36:19,677
Yes, I can see that now.

506
00:36:19,760 --> 00:36:23,139
At least I can kill you myself.

507
00:36:23,639 --> 00:36:26,225
What's this I'm hearing about?

508
00:36:26,309 --> 00:36:31,230
The girl you had murdered
13 years ago is still alive?!

509
00:36:31,314 --> 00:36:34,775
Is this Camia Cruz brouhaha
happening all over again?

510
00:36:35,610 --> 00:36:37,862
Yes, Papa. Lily Cruz is alive.

511
00:36:38,613 --> 00:36:42,158
How was I supposed to know
that girl had nine lives

512
00:36:42,241 --> 00:36:43,701
just like her mother?

513
00:36:44,952 --> 00:36:48,414
Emilia, you're this family's punch line.

514
00:36:48,497 --> 00:36:50,750
I don't know how you live with yourself.

515
00:36:51,792 --> 00:36:53,252
Papa, please.

516
00:36:53,878 --> 00:36:55,713
I don't need your insults right now.

517
00:36:55,796 --> 00:36:57,506
What I need from you is your support.

518
00:36:57,590 --> 00:37:01,135
This might affect Arnaldo's candidacy.

519
00:37:01,219 --> 00:37:05,223
Lily Cruz must be wiped off
the face of the earth!

520
00:37:07,099 --> 00:37:09,769
I need you to help me
and support me, Papa. Please.

521
00:37:10,853 --> 00:37:14,690
You are a hopeless case, my dear.

522
00:37:16,234 --> 00:37:17,902
Nothing is impossible, Papa.

523
00:37:18,277 --> 00:37:20,029
Well, come to think of it…

524
00:37:21,239 --> 00:37:23,991
Nothing's impossible
with someone like you.

525
00:37:24,784 --> 00:37:27,495
You know what you should do?
Go back to sleep.

526
00:37:28,871 --> 00:37:31,958
You might have left your brain
in your dreams.

527
00:37:57,066 --> 00:37:59,318
[young Lily wailing]

528
00:37:59,777 --> 00:38:01,654
<i>Mister, don't kill me!</i>

529
00:38:01,737 --> 00:38:03,698
-[gunshot]
-[loud scream]

530
00:38:03,781 --> 00:38:06,242
<i>Get up. Listen.</i>

531
00:38:06,325 --> 00:38:09,036
<i>You have to get away from here. Go.</i>

532
00:38:09,578 --> 00:38:14,709
<i>I've legally adopted you.</i>
<i>You'll be called Ivy Aguas.</i>

533
00:38:19,964 --> 00:38:22,383
<i>They can't learn the truth about Lily.</i>

534
00:38:23,718 --> 00:38:26,470
<i>They can't find out I am Lily.</i>

535
00:38:27,847 --> 00:38:29,765
<i>I need to speed up my plans.</i>

536
00:38:48,743 --> 00:38:52,204
[phone ringing]

537
00:38:54,040 --> 00:38:55,082
Hello, Ivy?

538
00:38:55,166 --> 00:38:56,292
[Arnaldo] Ivy? [knocks on door]

539
00:39:06,469 --> 00:39:07,845
Ivy? [knocks on door]

540
00:39:08,387 --> 00:39:09,305
Hon?

541
00:39:15,519 --> 00:39:16,979
-Are you okay?
-Hon?

542
00:39:17,480 --> 00:39:18,522
Yes.

543
00:39:18,981 --> 00:39:21,901
Shouldn't you be checking on your mom?

544
00:39:24,111 --> 00:39:25,738
How is she, by the way?

545
00:39:25,821 --> 00:39:28,282
Well, she's better than I expected.

546
00:39:30,826 --> 00:39:32,078
Hon, I'm just curious.

547
00:39:34,038 --> 00:39:35,081
What do you know about…

548
00:39:36,499 --> 00:39:37,625
Lily Cruz?

549
00:39:38,542 --> 00:39:39,710
What do you know about her?

550
00:39:40,378 --> 00:39:41,670
Actually, not much.

551
00:39:41,754 --> 00:39:45,841
The information just came from
Mom's mole in Diego's camp.

552
00:39:46,300 --> 00:39:48,761
Your mother's spy? Who could that be?

553
00:39:49,887 --> 00:39:50,971
I don't know.

554
00:39:51,055 --> 00:39:54,058
The truth is, I'm not convinced
that this Lily Cruz…

555
00:39:54,809 --> 00:39:57,436
is the one backing up Camia and Diego.

556
00:39:58,979 --> 00:40:01,273
And why not?

557
00:40:01,857 --> 00:40:04,193
Why should we be afraid
of someone who isn't here?

558
00:40:04,860 --> 00:40:06,779
She's nothing but an abstract idea.

559
00:40:07,571 --> 00:40:09,532
Mom and Camia are just being dramatic.

560
00:40:09,615 --> 00:40:13,077
And this Lily Cruz and
Diego too. They're pathetic.

561
00:40:15,746 --> 00:40:16,747
Hon, you should be careful.

562
00:40:17,331 --> 00:40:20,751
The people you underestimate
will never underestimate you.

563
00:40:22,169 --> 00:40:25,131
You never know,
it might cost us the election.

564
00:40:25,923 --> 00:40:26,924
[scoffs]

565
00:40:28,467 --> 00:40:29,552
I'm just saying.

566
00:40:30,928 --> 00:40:32,346
[quietly] Lily Cruz.

567
00:40:36,058 --> 00:40:37,059
Hello, Auntie?

568
00:40:37,393 --> 00:40:39,311
Ivy called me, but then she hung up.

569
00:40:39,770 --> 00:40:40,938
Have you talked to her?

570
00:40:41,355 --> 00:40:44,024
Diego. Lily confirmed…

571
00:40:44,108 --> 00:40:46,610
that Emilia planted a spy in our camp.

572
00:40:47,236 --> 00:40:48,946
And there's only one person I suspect.

573
00:40:49,405 --> 00:40:50,364
Is it Nimfa?

574
00:40:50,990 --> 00:40:52,241
She's the only one close to us…

575
00:40:52,324 --> 00:40:53,576
<i>who's acting strange.</i>

576
00:40:54,118 --> 00:40:56,036
Diego, we need to investigate her.

577
00:40:56,662 --> 00:40:57,538
Okay, Aunt Camia.

578
00:41:06,213 --> 00:41:08,591
[Marlon] Batch, this house is huge.

579
00:41:08,674 --> 00:41:10,384
It has three bedrooms.

580
00:41:11,302 --> 00:41:13,721
-Oh. Miss Loring, Mister Pandoy.
-Yes?

581
00:41:13,804 --> 00:41:15,639
You can stay here if you want to.

582
00:41:16,599 --> 00:41:17,683
[Diego] He's right, Nanny, Uncle.

583
00:41:17,766 --> 00:41:19,935
We should stay here for now.

584
00:41:20,019 --> 00:41:22,396
We can't live in a burned house anyway.

585
00:41:23,939 --> 00:41:28,277
You have a point. We'll stay
here so we can live together.

586
00:41:28,903 --> 00:41:34,074
We might overstay our welcome, though.

587
00:41:34,158 --> 00:41:36,494
We'll spend our time browsing
the Internet on this computer.

588
00:41:36,577 --> 00:41:37,411
[chuckles]

589
00:41:37,495 --> 00:41:38,954
-Mr. Pandoy.
-Yes?

590
00:41:39,038 --> 00:41:40,122
You can browse the Internet?

591
00:41:40,206 --> 00:41:41,457
Do you have that back on the farm?

592
00:41:41,540 --> 00:41:44,835
Well, times have changed.
You have to adapt.

593
00:41:44,919 --> 00:41:47,004
Wait, does this place have any Wi-Fi?

594
00:41:47,087 --> 00:41:48,088
-[laughs]
-Yes, we do.

595
00:41:48,172 --> 00:41:49,673
[Loring] Wi-Fi, you say?

596
00:41:49,757 --> 00:41:51,050
You might become engrossed in it.

597
00:41:51,133 --> 00:41:53,093
This is for office use only.

598
00:41:54,053 --> 00:41:56,472
Anyway, Diego, can you make me an account?

599
00:41:56,555 --> 00:41:58,641
-I want to use Facebook.
-[laughter]

600
00:41:58,724 --> 00:42:01,060
-Look at her!
-Of course, Nanny.

601
00:42:01,769 --> 00:42:03,812
[Camia] By the way, Diego…

602
00:42:04,730 --> 00:42:05,773
Thank you.

603
00:42:06,190 --> 00:42:09,026
You managed to enter a political party.

604
00:42:09,610 --> 00:42:13,447
So, I'm pretty sure
you'll become the governor.

605
00:42:14,532 --> 00:42:15,699
Thank you, Aunt Camia.

606
00:42:16,158 --> 00:42:20,371
That's why we have to work
harder together in the campaign.

607
00:42:20,955 --> 00:42:22,581
-Yes.
-Everyone, listen.

608
00:42:23,624 --> 00:42:26,418
What are your suggestions
to improve Ardiente?

609
00:42:26,752 --> 00:42:28,379
If you ask me, Diego…

610
00:42:28,462 --> 00:42:31,549
I wish our town could have
a bigger hospital,

611
00:42:31,632 --> 00:42:33,884
so the sick wouldn't have to travel far.

612
00:42:34,969 --> 00:42:36,470
-He's right.
-He's right.

613
00:42:36,554 --> 00:42:37,805
Hospital.

614
00:42:37,888 --> 00:42:40,766
[Camia] To avoid what happened
to Nimfa's father.

615
00:42:40,849 --> 00:42:42,518
-What?
-He was forced to leave…

616
00:42:42,601 --> 00:42:43,561
to treat his sickness.

617
00:42:44,103 --> 00:42:46,105
Nimfa, what was
your father's illness again?

618
00:42:46,188 --> 00:42:48,607
-[Loring] What?
-Uh…

619
00:42:50,067 --> 00:42:51,235
-I'm sorry?
-[Camia] Uh…

620
00:42:51,318 --> 00:42:53,988
Didn't you say you needed money
because your father was sick?

621
00:42:56,615 --> 00:42:59,410
Yes, ma'am. Um…

622
00:43:00,452 --> 00:43:01,870
He has kidney problems.

623
00:43:01,954 --> 00:43:03,414
-Why didn't we know about that?
-Fernan?

624
00:43:03,497 --> 00:43:04,790
Hold on, Nimfa.

625
00:43:05,165 --> 00:43:06,709
Where is your father staying, anyway?

626
00:43:07,084 --> 00:43:08,335
[suspenseful music]

627
00:43:08,419 --> 00:43:09,753
In Manila.

628
00:43:10,421 --> 00:43:13,048
Well… He's staying at my aunt's.

629
00:43:13,799 --> 00:43:15,718
Didn't I tell you that before?

630
00:43:15,801 --> 00:43:17,303
[indistinct chatter]

631
00:43:17,386 --> 00:43:19,888
Easy, guys. Easy.

632
00:43:19,972 --> 00:43:23,017
[Marlon] You know, she's been
stressed out by her family.

633
00:43:23,100 --> 00:43:24,602
Now, you're stressing her out too.

634
00:43:24,810 --> 00:43:28,105
Let's just focus on our campaign, okay?

635
00:43:28,188 --> 00:43:30,816
Who has any other suggestions
for our strategy?

636
00:43:30,899 --> 00:43:33,485
How about you? Nothing?

637
00:43:46,457 --> 00:43:49,251
[Claire] If we find out
who sent that check,

638
00:43:49,543 --> 00:43:51,211
then we can trace her location.

639
00:43:51,712 --> 00:43:54,798
Okay, Aunt Claire. Go ahead
and find Lily Cruz for me.

640
00:43:55,674 --> 00:43:56,967
-Thank you.
-Okay.

641
00:43:58,177 --> 00:44:00,095
-Eat your breakfast, okay?
-Thank you.

642
00:44:04,016 --> 00:44:06,060
-[Claire] Hey.
-[Ivy] Hi, Mamita.

643
00:44:06,602 --> 00:44:07,603
[smooches]

644
00:44:08,771 --> 00:44:10,314
Emilia, how are you?

645
00:44:11,023 --> 00:44:12,483
And what are you doing here?

646
00:44:15,361 --> 00:44:17,780
If you're both here to laugh at me,

647
00:44:17,863 --> 00:44:19,365
go ahead, have a laugh.

648
00:44:20,074 --> 00:44:23,118
But, one day, I'll prove
to you guys that I'm right.

649
00:44:23,452 --> 00:44:26,622
Lily Cruz is a threat
to our family and to this town.

650
00:44:27,164 --> 00:44:30,292
For all I know, your spy
in Diego's camp is wrong.

651
00:44:30,626 --> 00:44:32,628
How reliable is your intel, anyway?

652
00:44:32,711 --> 00:44:34,380
If you're just here to
lecture me like Papa,

653
00:44:34,463 --> 00:44:35,673
can you just leave?

654
00:44:39,551 --> 00:44:41,053
-Hon, excuse me.
-Yes.

655
00:44:43,555 --> 00:44:46,767
It's a good thing Arnaldo left,
so he won't have to hear this.

656
00:44:47,184 --> 00:44:50,646
Emilia, you're so weak.
You're pathetic and a coward.

657
00:44:52,940 --> 00:44:55,109
You know nothing about me, Ivy.

658
00:44:56,318 --> 00:44:58,362
[chuckles] Do you want to go shopping?

659
00:44:58,695 --> 00:45:00,447
Let's go shopping so that…

660
00:45:00,531 --> 00:45:02,699
you'll forget that Lily Cruz.

661
00:45:02,783 --> 00:45:04,326
So that you can move on.

662
00:45:04,410 --> 00:45:07,162
I can't move on from Lily Cruz.

663
00:45:07,871 --> 00:45:11,625
If I managed to get rid of her before,
I can do it again now.

664
00:45:12,960 --> 00:45:14,420
Why do you even care?

665
00:45:14,503 --> 00:45:17,506
Should Ivy Aguas be scared of

666
00:45:17,589 --> 00:45:18,799
Lily Cruz?

667
00:45:18,882 --> 00:45:21,510
[suspenseful music playing]

668
00:45:22,386 --> 00:45:23,595
[chuckles]

669
00:45:23,679 --> 00:45:25,639
I told you I'm not
scared of anything, remember?

670
00:45:25,722 --> 00:45:27,975
Not even you.

671
00:45:33,021 --> 00:45:33,939
Okay.

672
00:45:34,523 --> 00:45:37,985
Speaking as your friend, if you want,

673
00:45:38,068 --> 00:45:40,863
I can help you look for Lily Cruz.

674
00:45:40,946 --> 00:45:44,616
Really? Do you actually think
I'd still believe you

675
00:45:44,700 --> 00:45:47,494
after you maligned me
and the rest of the Ardientes?

676
00:45:48,162 --> 00:45:50,998
You shouldn't vent your anger
on me, Emilia.

677
00:45:51,081 --> 00:45:53,083
I am not Lily Cruz.

678
00:45:53,167 --> 00:45:55,502
Then why are you so defensive?

679
00:45:55,586 --> 00:45:57,296
And why can't you accept the fact

680
00:45:57,379 --> 00:46:02,176
that ever since you arrived in this town,
my family has been having problems?

681
00:46:02,759 --> 00:46:05,012
Hasn't your family always had them?

682
00:46:05,095 --> 00:46:08,015
Your lives are made of problems.

683
00:46:08,098 --> 00:46:10,934
Each and every one of you keeps
trying to bring each other down.

684
00:46:11,018 --> 00:46:14,021
Emilia, you allow your dad to insult you.

685
00:46:14,104 --> 00:46:16,648
You also believe anyone so easily.

686
00:46:20,736 --> 00:46:22,488
I'll find Lily Cruz

687
00:46:23,697 --> 00:46:25,824
no matter where she's hiding.

688
00:46:35,834 --> 00:46:37,002
<i>You need to mislead Emilia.</i>

689
00:46:37,085 --> 00:46:39,421
<i>She can't discover your true identity.</i>

690
00:46:39,505 --> 00:46:41,006
<i>We're going to hunt Lily Cruz.</i>

691
00:46:41,089 --> 00:46:42,508
[woman] <i>Haven't you heard?</i>

692
00:46:42,591 --> 00:46:46,178
<i>Emilia's nabbing all the women</i>
<i>who are the same age as Lily Cruz.</i>

693
00:46:46,261 --> 00:46:48,263
[Ivy] <i>What will you do to them?</i>
<i>Where are you taking them?</i>

694
00:46:48,347 --> 00:46:50,933
[Emilia] <i>I won't do anything</i>
<i>today that you won't like.</i>

695
00:46:52,267 --> 00:46:53,936
<i>-Lily, dear.</i>
<i>-Mom!</i>

696
00:46:54,853 --> 00:46:56,355
<i>Is Lily alive?! Where is she?!</i>

697
00:46:56,438 --> 00:46:59,233
-<i>Yes! My daughter is alive!</i>
-[Diego] <i>Let go of her!</i>

698
00:47:02,778 --> 00:47:05,822
[theme music playing]
